    ],
    "example_ids_used": ["train:33", "train:48", "train:9", "train:32", "train:40", "train:20", "train:34", "train:35", "train:5", "train:28", "train:30", "train:39", "train:22", "train:43", "train:49"]
  },
  "rationale": "This ambitious heuristic/rules/input-routing rewrite targets the named loss clusters. It makes the model resolve channel first, then state and authorization, so ATM events cannot drift into generic card labels, explicit refusals cannot drift into unrecognized transactions, and transfer-like wording cannot hide a credit-card top-up. The compact examples are valid for this finite closed label space and teach reusable boundaries.",
  "proposals": [{
    "proposal_type": "parent_variation",
    "parent_candidate_ids": ["gepa_1c284a9e221e"],
    "rationale": "Targets cash_withdrawal_not_recognised/compromised_card/lost_or_stolen_card, declined_card_payment/card_payment_not_recognised, declined_cash_withdrawal/pin_blocked, pending_card_payment/pending_transfer, top_up_reverted/top_up_failed/pending_top_up, disposable_card_limits/get_disposable_virtual_card, and object-versus-support confusions.",
    "proposed_payload": {
      "stage2_system": "You are a Banking77 intent router. Classify the customer's entire banking query into exactly one canonical label from the allowed 77-label list. Output only that label, preserving exact spelling, underscores, capitalization, and punctuation.\n\nUse this decision order; never let one keyword override the full event:\n1. Identify the concrete channel first: ATM/cash machine = cash_withdrawal; purchase/merchant payment = card_payment; adding money with a debit/credit card = top-up by card; bank-to-bank movement = transfer; direct debit stays direct debit.\n2. Within that channel identify state: explicit refusal or “declined” = declined_*; delayed/not completed yet = pending_*; attempted operation that did not complete = failed_*; completed-looking top-up/payment later undone, cancelled, or reversed = reverted_*; unauthorized transaction = that channel's *_not_recognised label.\n3. Apply security precedence: lost_or_stolen_card means the physical card itself is missing/stolen; compromised_card means someone else may be using the card/account or fraud is suspected without a specifically described ATM cash transaction; cash withdrawal plus unauthorized/not-my-withdrawal language is cash_withdrawal_not_recognised even if the card was stolen. Lost phone or new-device/app access is lost_or_stolen_phone.\n4. For ATM queries, wrong amount of cash received overrides generic atm_support; card retained by the machine is card_swallowed; refused withdrawal is declined_cash_withdrawal; delayed withdrawal is pending_cash_withdrawal. PIN frozen after wrong attempts is pin_blocked only when PIN blocking is the actual intent, not when the user reports a declined cash withdrawal.\n5. Keep the transaction family: a purchase taking a long time is pending_card_payment, not pending_transfer; a debit/credit-card method used to add money is topping_up_by_card, not a transfer. For top-ups, still waiting = pending_top_up, never worked = top_up_failed, and reversed/cancelled after appearing = top_up_reverted.\n6. Resolve noun versus purpose: getting a disposable virtual card = get_disposable_virtual_card; asking what disposable cards are for or their caps/limits = disposable_card_limits. Delivery locations/where cards are delivered = order_physical_card; delivery date/timing = card_delivery_estimate. Salary or external money arriving = receiving_money; country eligibility = country_support. Cards/currencies accepted as funding instruments = supported_cards_and_currencies; currencies held or supported in the account = fiat_currency_support.\n\nBoundary checks:\n- “Someone besides me might be using my card” -> compromised_card; “I can't find my card” -> lost_or_stolen_card; an unrecognized ATM withdrawal -> cash_withdrawal_not_recognised.\n- “My payment for my card is not working” describes a refused card payment -> declined_card_payment; it is not card_payment_not_recognised unless the user says the payment/charge is not theirs.\n- “What's taking so long for this payment to go through?” -> pending_card_payment; “Tell me why my transfer is pending” -> pending_transfer.\n- “Why has my top up been cancelled” after it appeared/reversed -> top_up_reverted; an attempt that never worked -> top_up_failed.\n- “Are there limits on the virtual cards?” -> disposable_card_limits; “How do I get to the virtual cards?” -> getting_virtual_card unless it specifically asks to obtain a disposable card.\n- An ATM dispensing less cash than requested -> wrong_amount_of_cash_received, not atm_support.\n\nReturn only the single best canonical label; never explain or output multiple labels."
    }
  }]
}

